Here are the exact locations of the "Memo" entity definition across all four layers in this repository:

---

## 1. SQL Schema (CREATE TABLE)

The `memo` table is defined in the LATEST.sql migration files for all three supported databases:

- **SQLite**: `/bench/repo/store/migration/sqlite/LATEST.sql` -- line 33
- **PostgreSQL**: `/bench/repo/store/migration/postgres/LATEST.sql` -- line 32
- **MySQL**: `/bench/repo/store/migration/mysql/LATEST.sql` -- line 32

All three define the same logical columns: `id`, `uid`, `creator_id`, `created_ts`, `updated_ts`, `row_status`, `content`, `visibility`, `pinned`, and `payload`. The differences are dialect-specific (e.g., `SERIAL` vs `AUTOINCREMENT`, `JSONB` vs `JSON` vs `TEXT`).

There are also numerous incremental migration files that alter the memo table across versions (e.g., `store/migration/sqlite/0.2/01__memo_visibility.sql`, `store/migration/sqlite/0.22/02__memo_payload.sql`, `store/migration/sqlite/0.24/00__memo.sql`, etc.).

---

## 2. Go Store Model (struct)

- **File**: `/bench/repo/store/memo.go` -- line 35

```go
type Memo struct {
	ID         int32
	UID        string
	RowStatus  RowStatus
	CreatorID  int32
	CreatedTs  int64
	UpdatedTs  int64
	Content    string
	Visibility Visibility
	Pinned     bool
	Payload    *storepb.MemoPayload
	ParentUID  *string
}
```

The same file also contains companion types `FindMemo` (line 57) and related query/filter structs.

---

## 3. API Protobuf Message

- **File**: `/bench/repo/proto/api/v1/memo_service.proto` -- line 198

The `message Memo` defines the API-level representation with fields: `name`, `state`, `creator`, `create_time`, `update_time`, `content`, `visibility`, `tags`, `pinned`, `attachments`, `relations`, `reactions`, `property`, and `parent`. It uses Google API resource annotations (`google.api.resource`) to declare the resource pattern `memos/{memo}`.

There is also a store-layer protobuf file at `/bench/repo/proto/store/memo.proto` which defines `message MemoPayload` (line 7) -- this is not the Memo entity itself but the payload sub-message used by the Go store struct's `Payload` field.

---

## 4. Generated Frontend TypeScript Types

- **File**: `/bench/repo/web/src/types/proto/api/v1/memo_service_pb.ts` -- line 79

```typescript
export type Memo = Message<"memos.api.v1.Memo"> & {
  name: string;
  state: State;
  creator: string;
  createTime?: Timestamp | undefined;
  updateTime?: Timestamp | undefined;
  content: string;
  visibility: Visibility;
  tags: string[];
  pinned: boolean;
  attachments: Attachment[];
  relations: MemoRelation[];
  reactions: Reaction[];
  property?: Memo_Property | undefined;
  parent?: string | undefined;
  // ...
};
```

The corresponding schema constant `MemoSchema` is declared at line 196 of the same file (`export const MemoSchema: GenMessage<Memo>`).

